  "claim": "Paul Shaw wrote a book on the history of the design of the New York subway system in 2014 for a magazine. That magazine and National Journal are not both periodicals.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Print (magazine). Sentence: Print, A Quarterly Journal of the Graphic Arts was a limited edition quarterly periodical begun in 1940 and continued under different names up to the present day as Print, a bimonthly American magazine about visual culture and design.\nPage: National Journal. Sentence: National Journal is a research and advisory services company based in Washington, D.C. offering services in government affairs, advocacy communications and policy brands research for government and business leaders.\nPage: National Journal. Sentence: It publishes daily journalism covering politics and public policy and is led by President Kevin Turpin and Editor-in-Chief Stephen G. Smith.\nPage: Paul Shaw (design historian). Sentence: He has written a book on the history of the design of the New York subway system, \"Helvetica and the New York Subway System: The True (Maybe) Story\", on the work of William Addison Dwiggins, and for \"Print\" magazine.",
